    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who provides the highest efficiency score of 82.08. Facing Rod\u00f3n, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable park factor and a strong xwOBA of 0.376, pushing his valuation well into the \"Strong\" start tier despite the lefty-lefty matchup. Following him in reliability are **Nolan Schanuel** (64.30) and **Josh Lowe** (64.95), both of whom take advantage of a generous 4.60 xERA from Luis Severino. While **Josh Lowe** is projected at the bottom of the order, his dynamic platoon advantage against the right-handed arm makes him a high-floor play today.\n\nRegarding roster flexibility, **Nasim Nunez** (51.41) and **Liam Hicks** (54.43) occupy marginal territory but remain in the lineup due to the scarcity of viable alternatives. **Nasim Nunez** faces a tough defensive matchup against a quick-to-the-plate catcher, which tempers his stolen base upside; however, his switch-hitting profile provides just enough cushion to clear the bench threshold. The most difficult decision rested on **Dominic Smith** (53.57); while he sits at the low end of our starting criteria, his favorable platoon split against Alcantara keeps him ahead of our deeper bench assets. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Lowe**, as both are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Should their actual batting orders drop significantly\u2014particularly for **Josh Lowe**\u2014we may see their scores dip closer to the 40-point floor. Fortunately, our core remains intact, though the absence of **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014who remain off the active slate due to off-days or injury\u2014limits our ceiling today. Keep a close eye on the weather and official confirmations for **Liam Hicks** to ensure he stays atop the order as anticipated.",
